## 4. Key Takeaways & Recommendations
1. Document the event as an Amoxicillin-induced cutaneous drug reaction (Probable).
2. Update the patient's medical record with an alert for beta-lactam / penicillin allergy.
3. Submit the ICSR (Individual Case Safety Report) to the Pharmacovigilance Programme of India (PvPI).
